    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.\n\n[PEP 798](https://peps.python.org/pep-0798/) in Py3.15 adds unpacking in comprehensions:\n```cython\nresult = [*many for many in values]\n```\n\n\n### Describe the solution you'd like.\n\nThe list comprehension case essentially replaces `PyList_Append()` with `PyList_Extend()` (or an optimised variant). Set and dict comprehensions should be equally easy to do using `Py*_Update()`.\n\nGenerator expressions are quite a different thing. But we might be able to do this entirely at the node level, injecting another nested for-loop level. That might be a separate PR to the C code changes for comprehensions.\n\nNote the reasons why `yield from` semantics were explicitly not chosen for generator expressions:\nhttps://peps.python.org/pep-0798/#appendix-semantics-of-generator-delegation\n\nThe comprehensions seem a good first issue target, assuming a bit of C knowledge.\nLook for the `ListCompAppend` utility code and its usages in `ExprNodes.py` to get started.\n\n### Describe alternatives you've considered.\n\n_No response_\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_",
