        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "I'd like to work on the list, set, and dict comprehension part of this.\n\nI confirmed that current `master` rejects the new syntax and that the existing `listcomp`, `setcomp`, and `dictcomp` tests pass on both C and C++ backends. My plan is to represent top-level `*`/`**` comprehension expressions as update operations, using list extend, set update, and dict update while preserving the existing comprehension evaluation order. I'll add run tests for all three forms, including filtering, nested loops, duplicate dict keys, and invalid inputs.\n\nI'll leave generator-expression semantics to a separate follow-up, as suggested in the issue.\n",
